    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d638">

                <pb facs="0803" n="709" sameAs="frus:frus1896/pg709"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Rockhill to Mr. Lee.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1896-10-08"><hi rendition="#italic">October 8,
                        1896</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The Department has received your dispatch
                    No. 160, of the 3d instant, with inclosure, relative to the fate of Charles
                    Govin, and in reply you are informed that your action in demanding of the
                    Governor and Captain General of Cuba the name of the subordinate general who
                    made the report of the death of Mr. Govin and the name of the place at which it
                    was written is approved by the Department.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">* * * * * * *</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">W. W. Rockhill.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
